    {
      "name": "enumerateScanners",
      "params": [],
      "returns": {
        "k": "ref",
        "name": "EnumerateScannersResult"
      },
      "promise": true,
      "comment": "Android only. DataWedge may omit `COMMAND_IDENTIFIER` on query replies. The plugin accepts\nidentifier-free replies only when the payload matches exactly one pending call that expects the\nsame result payload shape. Avoid overlapping pending calls that share that shape. When sender\nidentity is unavailable (Android API 24 to 33, or API 34+ when the platform withholds it),\nmatching identifier-free replies are accepted for compatibility. If a call times out, a delayed\nidentifier-free reply can still match a later sequential call that expects the same shape and\nresolve it with stale data. This default may change in the next Capacitor major version; see\nhttps://github.com/Cap-go/capacitor-zebra-datawedge/issues/25/."
    },
